  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Access to Housing and Basic Services for People Fleeing the Conflict in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention is responding to the emergency resulting from the invasion of Ukraine by the Russian army, which began on 24 February 2022 and is ongoing. As of 29 May, more than 6.7 million refugees have fled Ukraine to other countries in Europe, while more than 252,000 third country nationals have fled the country as of 25 May. As it becomes evident that the fighting and damage to housing and infrastructure in Ukraine will not allow for a sustainable return anytime soon, IOM, through this project, is looking to provide longer-term solutions in Hungary for people fleeing the conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
